<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Acesita H1 net vs loss.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Acesita H1 net vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian private steelmaker Acesita SA on Monday issued the following statement on its first-half results:</p>
<p>			 H1 1997	 H1 1996</p>
<p>    Net		  13.2 million	39.2 million loss</p>
<p>    Oper. profit     13.7 million	50.6 million loss</p>
<p>    Net oper. revs  276.6 million     280.3 million</p>
<p>Note: All figures in Brazilian reais, not adjusted for inflation. When adjusted for inflation, Acesita's first-half net profit was 40.9 million reais, against a loss of 31.6 million reais in the same period of last year, the company said.  </p>
<p>Acesita said steel output fell to 252,447 tonnes from 252,137 in the same period a year ago. Sales of steel products rose 5.2 percent to 267,471 tonnes.</p>
<p>Domestic sales increased 24 percent, accounting for 88 percent of the total, it said.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
